From: Alan Shearer
Subject: udp: skip software TX checksum when the route is loopback

SendRoutedData always walks the datagram to compute the UDP
pseudo-header checksum, then sets NET_BUFFER_L4_CHECKSUM_VALID so the
receive path will skip verification.

On loopback the packet never leaves the host. The software checksum is
pure CPU and shows up on localhost iperf3 -u. If the route's interface
has IFF_LOOPBACK, leave udp_checksum at the 0 already written before
Sync() and only set L4_VALID. Deframe already skips the check when that
flag is set.

IPv6 UDP requires a non-zero checksum on the wire; loopback is not on
the wire. The L4_VALID flag is what the local Deframe path consults.

Ticket: https://dev.haiku-os.org/ticket/18730

---

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
@@ -1078,12 +1078,25 @@
 
 	header.Sync();
 
-	uint16 calculatedChecksum = Checksum::PseudoHeader(AddressModule(),
-		gBufferModule, buffer, IPPROTO_UDP);
-	if (calculatedChecksum == 0)
-		calculatedChecksum = 0xffff;
-
-	*UDPChecksumField(buffer) = calculatedChecksum;
+	const bool loopback = route != NULL
+		&& route->interface_address != NULL
+		&& route->interface_address->interface != NULL
+		&& (route->interface_address->interface->flags & IFF_LOOPBACK) != 0;
+
+	if (!loopback) {
+		uint16 calculatedChecksum = Checksum::PseudoHeader(AddressModule(),
+			gBufferModule, buffer, IPPROTO_UDP);
+		if (calculatedChecksum == 0)
+			calculatedChecksum = 0xffff;
+
+		*UDPChecksumField(buffer) = calculatedChecksum;
+	}
+	// else: udp_checksum is already 0 from the prepend above. Packet never
+	// leaves the host; Deframe honors NET_BUFFER_L4_CHECKSUM_VALID on RX.
+
 	buffer->buffer_flags |= NET_BUFFER_L4_CHECKSUM_VALID;
 
 	return next->module->send_routed_data(next, route, buffer);
 }
